+## Adjudication
+
+Agree: honest options, refusal of absent hardening/LTO, artifact tests,
+per-sample correctness, mutation controls, scoped measurements and open-only
+backlog. The original backlog is archived unchanged (SHA-256
+162c96a429bc321763398a8cd09bec6f026352626ab8a17d2958bcd156d1cea1).
+
+Disagree with copying the supplied baseline as current facts. In particular,
+CPU runtime detection is already implemented. Folding cpu_supports true from
+-march is conceptually wrong: permission to emit an ISA is not the CPU being
+queried. Retain runtime semantics; investigate races and residual cost separately.
+PIE defaults are platform/product policy, not universal GCC semantics.
+The proposed stack-probe 1-KiB exception needs a guard-gap proof, and canary
+layout needs an address-direction proof. _Float16/__bf16 must not be conflated
+with mandatory C23 completeness. Percentage/size goals without a measured
+workload denominator are hypotheses, not acceptance evidence.
+
+## Red-team findings and changes
+
+1. Merely forwarding no_builtins into sema is insufficient. The post-inline
+   strlen pass independently folded ordinary names. It now receives the mode.
+2. Math simplification and external purity inference were independent bypasses:
+   sqrt could become an instruction and unused strlen could disappear under
+   -fno-builtin. Math folding now uses a scoped thread-local policy restored
+   even on early returns; purity inference receives the TU policy explicitly.
+   Source-declared pure/const and inferred user-body properties remain valid.
+3. Unknown -f flags must fail regardless of -v order. The fallback now has
+   explicit no-op/refused entries, including LTO/ASan and other security families.
+   This is NOT a complete generated registry: all existing stateful arms and
+   unknown -mno/-W paths still need the MB-01 inventory follow-up.
+4. Freestanding mode changes __STDC_HOSTED__ and ordinary aliases; explicit
+   compiler builtin interfaces remain. Partial builtin/vectorizer controls are
+   refused rather than pretending independent support. Full tree-vectorize
+   disable gates map, SLP, memory/SSA ARX and interleaving entries.
+5. Static strlen literal folding also appears to count beyond an embedded NUL.
+   Static initializer default-mode lowering previously panicked in the earlier
+   session. These need permanent witnesses; neither is closed by the VLA fix.
+
+## Measurement boundaries
+
+Current reconstructed fastbuild succeeds with warnings denied. The initial
+focused hosted/VLA/option tests passed. An additional sqrt/unused-strlen probe
+now retains both ordinary calls under -fno-builtin.
+GCC16.2/Clang23.1.0/CE ICX-channel comparison was run using the repository oracle
+on this probe: root instruction counts local 4, remote 1 each (tail-call shape).
+This is NOT a runtime win and the moving ICX alias does not establish 2026.1.1.
+The exact required KERNEL.c oracle command failed because that file is missing;
+no substitute is relabeled as the requested gate.
+
+Final test, mutation and profiling outcomes are recorded separately below when
+completed. Whole-programme completion and beating all compilers are not claimed.
+
+## Fresh validation and adversarial follow-through
+
+- First reconstructed FAST: **250 passed, 25 failed, 6 slow gates skipped**;
+  4,963 Rust tests passed, 9 ignored. Strict Clippy and rustfmt passed.
+  Failures were retained, not converted to skips: GCC16 absent, new gate's
+  accidental double-backslash, hosted parity missing and unsupported
+  -freg-struct-return used by an older argument-ABI fixture.
+- Installed native GCC/G++16.2.0-3 and matching multilib. Its first -m32
+  execution crashed with BFD2.44 despite successful linking. Inspected the PLT
+  disassembly before upgrading BFD to2.47; the same hello-world now exits0.
+  No LLD workaround or fake GCC-version wrapper was used. GCC14 multilib,
+  AArch64/RISC-V cross toolchains, Valgrind3.24 and active8-GiB swap are present.
+- Corrected the shell continuation and added the hosted workflow invocation;
+  CI parity now passes. -freg-struct-return is explicitly refused: the older
